+# Contributing to e164.it
+
+Thanks for your interest in contributing to **e164.it** — an E.164 phone number parsing & CSV batch normalization toolkit (UI + API).
+
+This repository aims to stay **small, readable, and operationally predictable**: minimal dependencies, clear behavior, and stable outputs.
+
+---
+
+## What you can contribute
+
+- **Bug reports** (UI, API, batch parsing, edge cases)
+- **Docs improvements** (examples, wording, clarifications)
+- **UI/UX improvements** (copy, tooltips, accessibility)
+- **API improvements** (validation, error handling, OpenAPI accuracy)
+- **Security & privacy improvements** (see Security below)
+
+If you plan a larger change, open an issue first to align on approach.
+
+---
+
+## Ground rules (project principles)
+
+1. **Predictable outputs** over cleverness.
+2. **Minimal dependencies** (avoid adding frameworks/build systems unless truly necessary).
+3. **Privacy-aware defaults** (masking/hashing must remain safe and explicit).
+4. **Docs and UI must match behavior** (especially auth/rate-limit semantics).
+
+---
+
+## Development setup
+
+### Requirements
+
+- **Node.js 22** (see `.nvmrc` / `.node-version`)
+- npm
+
+### Install
+
+```bash
+npm ci
+```
+
+### Build metadata
+
+This repo generates a small `public/build-meta.js` file used by the UI (commit SHA/link):
+
+```bash
+npm run build
+```
+
+---
+
+## Running locally
+
+### UI-only (static preview)
+
+If you only work on `public/` pages (HTML/CSS/JS), any static server is fine:
+
+```bash
+python -m http.server --directory public 8080
+# open http://localhost:8080
+```
+
+Note: this will not run `/v1/*` API endpoints locally.
+
+### Full stack (UI + Cloudflare Pages Functions)
+
+This project uses **Cloudflare Pages Functions** (`functions/`) and Wrangler (`wrangler.toml`).
+
+A typical local dev command is:
+
+```bash
+npx wrangler pages dev public
+```
+
+Depending on what you touch, you may need bindings:
+- **D1** database binding: `DB`
+- **KV** namespace binding: `RL`
+
+If you don’t have Cloudflare credentials/bindings available, you can still contribute UI and docs changes without running the full stack locally.
+
+---
+
+## Configuration notes (secrets & bindings)
+
+### Secrets
+
+Never commit secrets.
+
+- `HASH_SECRET` is required to enable stable HMAC hashing.
+- Admin endpoints require an admin token (see `.github/SECURITY.md` for reporting; do not post tokens in issues).
+
+In production, store secrets with Wrangler, e.g.:
+
+```bash
+wrangler secret put HASH_SECRET
+```
+
+### Database migrations (D1)
+
+Schema migrations live in `migrations/`.
+
+When you introduce schema changes:
+1. Add a new migration file with the next number (e.g. `0002_...sql`)
+2. Keep migrations **idempotent** where possible (`IF NOT EXISTS`, etc.)
+3. Document behavior changes in the PR description
+
+---
+
+## Testing / sanity checks
+
+Automated tests are intentionally minimal.
+
+Before opening a PR, please run:
+
+```bash
+npm ci
+node -e "import('./functions/v1/parse.js'); import('./functions/v1/batch/parse.js'); console.log('ok')"
+```
+
+Optional: if you have access to a deployed instance and credentials, you can run the smoke script:
+
+```bash
+BASE_URL="https://e164.it" API_KEY="e164_..." ADMIN_TOKEN="..." bash scripts/test_api.sh
+```
+
+Do **not** paste real keys/tokens in issues or PRs.
+
+---
+
+## Code style
+
+- Follow `.editorconfig` (2-space indent, LF, final newline).
+- Prefer **plain, readable JavaScript** (ESM).
+- Keep the UI vanilla: small JS files, no heavy front-end frameworks.
+- Avoid changing output field names unless absolutely necessary (compatibility).
+
+---
+
+## Documentation rules
+
+If you change behavior, update documentation in the same PR:
+
+- `public/docs/`
+- `public/api/`
+- `public/api-docs/` (Swagger UI)
+- `functions/v1/openapi.json.js` (OpenAPI generator)
+
+Important: the OpenAPI spec, docs pages, and middleware behavior must remain consistent.
+
+---
+
+## Submitting a pull request
+
+1. Create a branch from `main`.
+2. Keep PRs focused (one feature/fix per PR where possible).
+3. Include:
+   - What changed and why
+   - Screenshots for UI changes (before/after)
+   - Any new limits/behavior changes
+4. Ensure checks pass (CI imports key modules).
+
+### Commit messages
+
+Use concise, imperative messages, e.g.:
+
+- `Fix batch CSV delimiter autodetect`
+- `Docs: clarify hosted API key requirement`
+- `UI: improve API key tooltip and link`
+
+---
+
+## Security
+
+Please **do not open public issues** for security problems.
+
+Use GitHub’s **Private Vulnerability Reporting** or contact the maintainer as described in:
+
+- `.github/SECURITY.md`
+
